{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949505-hack-removing-lineages","id":949505,"title":"[Hack] Removing Lineages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-12T13:44:11-07:00","id":949505,"title":"[Hack] Removing Lineages","content":"So, finishing up chapter three, and I'm getting the distinct feeling that Lineage doesn't really <i>do</i> much. Mechanically speaking, they give you two Bestowments to choose from, and a Humor, which determines the element you need to sleep near to recover Pyros, and seems kind of like it's supposed to determine your aTorment, but then Torment is the Vice replacement and doesn't seem to actually be tied to Lineage. I guess your Humour is supposed to flavor the way your individual Tpent is expressed, rather than determining specifically what your Torment is.<br /> <br /> That seems pretty barebones for an X-Splat. Lineages fill a bit more of a narrative role, specifying the process by which Prometheans of the Lineages are created, and adding some details like Tammuz' relationship with language, but overall I'm not convinced Promethean needs X-Splats. Heck, it doesn't even really have Y-Splats in the traditional sense, with Refinements are supposed to be something you regularly change. So why not take it a step further and make Promethean the Splatless line?<br /> <br /> The Extempore give us a model of what Prometheans might look like if we removed Lineages. Work with your Storyteller to determine what process went into creating you, and pick an appropriate Bestowment to your Creation from among the 14 examples or use them as guidelines to create your own. Pick an appropriate Humour from among the examples (the four traditional Humours, plus Ectoplasm/Ephemera and Oil) or create your own using the examples as guidelines. Your Humour determines what element you need to sleep near to regain Pyros and flavors your Torment. <br /> <br /> The most significant difference I see this making is that you could have stitched-together Prometheans Creating robot Prometheans, Prometheans buried in earth and bound by words creating Prometheans by covering bodies in spirit-stuff, Egyptian-style Prometheans creating Greek-style Prometheans, and any combination in-between with Extempore popping up left and right. I think I'm ok with that implication, though.<br /> <br /> Is there anything I'm overlooking? Any important part of Promethean's themes I'd be leaving out by running everyone like Extempore? Any suggestions for how to refine or improve this idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-12-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:50:38-07:00","id":949509,"title":"","content":"I like it because it reinforces the lonely nature of Promethean existence; each and every one of them feels unique among their kind, and will likely never see another Created exactly like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:57:39-07:00","id":949512,"title":"","content":"Sounds right to me. I've always felt Lineages should be a DIY sort to thing. The only real risk I could see would be removing things like two Frankenstein meeting and learning that, even though they are the same, they are different. But the hack doesn't prevent that, if anything it makes the meeting more special, because there aren't a dozen more Franksteins paling around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:38:21-07:00","id":949618,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything wrong with the idea of stripping out Lineages. Their best use is for new players to grasp what ideas are in play in the setting, or to reference their legends. They're also great for letting a creature that begins as <i>tabula rasas</i> to have a sense of identity. If you think your players are going to fill in the gaps themselves, then you'll probably lose little of value.<br /> <br /> That said, I do like Lineages. As someone who fell head over heels in love with PtC1E, I felt they had a huge part in selling the game to me. 2E seems to dispense with a lot of this stuff, but I was a fan of how the details of each creation ritual and the stories and legends of each Lineage connected them deeply to the mythology. Almost every Promethean could draw a heritage all the way back to a single act of divine inspiration that rivaled the creation of Adam, and existed as proof of the Principle. Just as important was the unspoken use of &quot;lineage&quot; not just in the familial sense, but in a classical sense of scientists and philosophers forming a lineage of tutelage (Socrates instructed Plato, and Plato Aristotle, and so forth). Roots like these legitimized the Pilgrimage more than Azothic Memory does, in my reading, but it is what it is, and much of how Lineage and Humor was reflected externally is gone now, making Lineage more ornamental than iconic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:36:05-07:00","id":949858,"title":"","content":"You missed Disquiet/Wasteland expression.<br /> <br /> But yeah. Promethean isn't really about what you are, but how you get where you're going, so it makes sense that their X-axis is pretty barebones. It would be reasonable for every Promethean to be Extempore, mechanically; I'd personally keep them, mostly because I like the flavor and a finite set of choices at chargen is something I prefer because I go by the &quot;constraint breeds creativity&quot; school of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:18:39-07:00","id":955719,"title":"","content":"A quote by Matt in another thread got me thinking about expanding this hack:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954321-honest-question-what-do-you-think-about-disquiet?p=955509#post955509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The punch line, of course, is that as people our &amp;quot;Pilgrimage&amp;quot; never stops - you never stop learning, you never stop growing, or if you do, that's not good. Prometheans, in that way, have it a little easier; their story ends when they reach the New Dawn, or at least becomes a radically different story.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This leads me to wonder, what it would do to the game if the New Dawn wasn't a known thing. If all Prometheans struggled with the Extempore's lack of direction from Azothic Memory and uncertainty in if they would ever be able to complete the Great Work.<br /> <br /> I always liked that in Fullmetal Alchemist, the Elrics had no idea if it would ever actually be possible to get their bodies back. But they kept trying anyway, because they had to believe it was to keep themselves going. I've always kind of thought of the New Dawn similarly. Not something you know you can achieve if you follow the right steps, but an ongoing process that may or may not have an actual end.<br /> <br /> The Extempore serve this vision of the Pilgromage quite well. Between this, and my earlier musings on how I might like to make all Prometheans work like them mechanically... It seems like they just do the parts of Promethean that I like best better than the Lineages do. So, I'm considering just hacking Lineages out entirely and saying everyone is Extempore. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:30:39-07:00","id":955739,"title":"","content":"Bare bones for an x-splat? Ha! Geist and Demon have worse - they get one affinity power at Char Gen, and no extra charge for non-affinity powers after, and that's about it. Its especially notable in Demon to the point that the game acknowledges that its entirely in the Unchained's heads, completely an artificial divide with no meaning. And Lineage has a huge impact on Disquiet, Torment, and Wastelands as well as Bestowments, none of which should not be underestimated.<br /> <br /> To be honest, though? You don't need x-splats in any game, easily fixed through a simple houserule. Its simplicity within itself to remove clans, there's been plenty of methods to remove Paths in Mage, and so on. However, x-splats exist for a reason - they're easily recognizable archetypes that resonate along common tropes for people to engage in, which does help people when they're understanding and interacting with the game. It helps them engage with the story. That's the main benefit in any game - easily recognizable tropes that can be evoked for story reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:34:53-07:00","id":955743,"title":"","content":"I think it's a cool dichotomy because 1st edition acted like the New Dawn was a myth that most Promethean were pursuing, so it was really a game about hope, but some players felt like they were working towards a red herring.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition makes the pilgrimage a lot more real and guided, allowing the players to feel like they are progressing, but turning the game into a path that must be followed.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>, I think your hack would work perfectly to recreate the feelings of the 1st edition, and if your players want to embark on that journey, go right ahead, just be aware that some might lose hope somewhere along the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:46:23-07:00","id":955755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949505-hack-removing-lineages?p=955719#post955719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A quote by Matt in another thread got me thinking about expanding this hack:<br /> <br /> <br /> This leads me to wonder, what it would do to the game if the New Dawn wasn't a known thing. If all Prometheans struggled with the Extempore's lack of direction from Azothic Memory and uncertainty in if they would ever be able to complete the Great Work.<br /> <br /> I always liked that in Fullmetal Alchemist, the Elrics had no idea if it would ever actually be possible to get their bodies back. But they kept trying anyway, because they had to believe it was to keep themselves going. I've always kind of thought of the New Dawn similarly. Not something you know you can achieve if you follow the right steps, but an ongoing process that may or may not have an actual end.<br /> <br /> The Extempore serve this vision of the Pilgromage quite well. Between this, and my earlier musings on how I might like to make all Prometheans work like them mechanically... It seems like they just do the parts of Promethean that I like best better than the Lineages do. So, I'm considering just hacking Lineages out entirely and saying everyone is Extempore. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it!<br /> <br /> Personally though, I'm inclined to go the other way: instead of removing Lineages from Prometheans the way 2e removed Mockeries from Pandorans, I'd like to see Bestowments expanded into something more, subsuming 1e's Promethean Boons and other nuggets of power into a power structure not unlike 1e's Transmutations but organized around the Lineages instead of the Refinements. Heck, this could be a way to reintroduce some of 1e's Transmutations that didn't make it into 2e's more rigid Transmutation structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:47:07-07:00","id":955757,"title":"","content":"How would this work with Throngs? It is the only other aspect I can think involves Lineages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:57:52-07:00","id":955765,"title":"","content":"I think Humours and Elements should still be a thing; just make them more freeform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:09:34-07:00","id":955767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949505-hack-removing-lineages?p=955743#post955743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a cool dichotomy because 1st edition acted like the New Dawn was a myth that most Promethean were pursuing, so it was really a game about hope, but some players felt like they were working towards a red herring.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition makes the pilgrimage a lot more real and guided, allowing the players to feel like they are progressing, but turning the game into a path that must be followed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is really interesting. I never read 1e, just the opening fiction and first chapter, and I always had the impression that the New Dawn was semi-mythical. But when I read how well-defined it is in 2e, I assumed I had just misinterpreted the little of 1e that I had read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949505-hack-removing-lineages?p=955743#post955743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, I think your hack would work perfectly to recreate the feelings of the 1st edition, and if your players want to embark on that journey, go right ahead, just be aware that some might lose hope somewhere along the road.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would be my biggest concern about this hack. Hope can only take you so far before it starts to seem like you're just chasing a dream. I think 2e's Pilgrimage as an Integrity stat will help combat that despair somewhat, though. Hitting the milestones and seeing the little progress bar go up will, I think, make it feel a bit more &quot;real&quot; for the player, even if in-character there's no Azothic Memory telling them they're getting closer and no guarantee there's an end to get closer to. That's my hope, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:10:39-07:00","id":955768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949505-hack-removing-lineages?p=955765#post955765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Humours and Elements should still be a thing; just make them more freeform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, they would be in my take. You can pick one of the existing ones or work with the ST to create a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:23:59-07:00","id":955777,"title":"","content":"And they needn't be bundled together the way they are in the Lineages: just because Frankenstein bundles the Choleric Humour together with the Fire Element, that doesn't mean that <i>every</i> Promethean with a Choleric Humour has Fire as its Element. <br /> <br /> The way I'd handle it is that Humour influences the Promehean's personality and social interactions, while Element deals with the physical world: e.g., Humour defines in broad strokes Torment and Disquiet, while Element defines manner of recharging and nature of Wasteland. As for the Torment Anchor, that influences <i>what causes</i> Torment, whereas the Humour defines <i>how the Promethean responds</i> to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:40:05-07:00","id":955900,"title":"","content":"I'd be totally in favor, actually. I like the idea that every Promethean is essentially unique; even two Created made by the same ritual are going to experience the Pilgrimage very differently, and that's really the important thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}